(5027555, 732147, 30982, '<td valign="top">Alvin is indeed quite adorable, and he fetched you a very nice score!  I really appreciate you sharing the story and your editing details, though I''ll admit I''m not entirely sure (OK, completely not sure) I could re-create what you did.  I have no idea what lab sharpen is, nor how you blended the different tifs together.  You should make a tutorial!</td>', 'Alvin is indeed quite adorable, and he fetched you a very nice score!  I really appreciate you sharing the story and your editing details, though I''ll admit I''m not entirely sure (OK, completely not sure) I could re-create what you did.  I have no idea what lab sharpen is, nor how you blended the different tifs together.  You should make a tutorial!', '2008-10-27 15:50:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(5027560, 732163, 3746, '<td valign="top">I knew you''d have something up your sleeve.. great shot and well done on the ribbon.</td>', 'I knew you''d have something up your sleeve.. great shot and well done on the ribbon.', '2008-10-27 15:52:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(5027573, 732188, 18450, '<td valign="top">Beautiful shot, full of life and energy!</td>', 'Beautiful shot, full of life and energy!', '2008-10-27 16:04:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(5027582, 732247, 61651, '<td valign="top">Congratulations, Karen - this was one of my 10s and a favorite for the challenge.  Really well-done handling of DOF.  Great good luck with the composition too, to have them all more or less looking forward at you like that, with that frontrunner''s enigmatic expression - lends a weirdness to it, like we just might be in danger from them.</td>', 'Congratulations, Karen - this was one of my 10s and a favorite for the challenge.  Really well-done handling of DOF.  Great good luck with the composition too, to have them all more or less looking forward at you like that, with that frontrunner''s enigmatic expression - lends a weirdness to it, like we just might be in danger from them.', '2008-10-27 16:10:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(5027585, 731582, 82104, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your top ten placing, I think this picture is superb, I had it down for a ribbon.</td>', 'Congratulations on your top ten placing, I think this picture is superb, I had it down for a ribbon.', '2008-10-27 16:11:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(5027595, 732163, 12223, '<td valign="top">Having shot a few Eagles myself, this is a wonderful capture.  Clean crisp and detailed.  Well done.</td>', 'Having shot a few Eagles myself, this is a wonderful capture.  Clean crisp and detailed.  Well done.', '2008-10-27 16:16:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(5027606, 732247, 58452, '<td valign="top">Wow! Beautiful use of DOF.  Someone wanted to know what those gulls were thinking.   <u><b> MINE!</b></u></td>', 'Wow! Beautiful use of DOF.  Someone wanted to know what those gulls were thinking.    MINE!', '2008-10-27 16:24:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(5027623, 732144, 69668, '<td valign="top">Lucky you to have found this little guy/girl.  So where is the best place to find deer around here?  I have only spotted several here and there.</td>', 'Lucky you to have found this little guy/girl.  So where is the best place to find deer around here?  I have only spotted several here and there.', '2008-10-27 16:33:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(5027670, 731987, 45475, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Prash:</b></div><hr/><i> Also, just to clarify, if a wildlife challenge happens again in future, with the same description, I will run to the zoo again.. unless the description clearly states ''no zoo pictures allowed''. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Good on ya, me too! Not that mine was at a zoo, just that I have absolutely no problem with it and would do it myself next time.<br/> <br/>As for the photo, I think <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=91527" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Jessi</a> pretty much sums up all the technical/editing issues I had with it also. Those "smudgy" bits she refers to look like spot blurring to me. Not sure what monitor you''re using and you may not be seeing it so obviously, but it might pay to look at your image on other screens just to be sure, before uploading :)</td>', 'Originally posted by Prash: Also, just to clarify, if a wildlife challenge happens again in future, with the same description, I will run to the zoo again.. unless the description clearly states ''no zoo pictures allowed''.   Good on ya, me too! Not that mine was at a zoo, just that I have absolutely no problem with it and would do it myself next time. As for the photo, I think  Jessi pretty much sums up all the technical/editing issues I had with it also. Those "smudgy" bits she refers to look like spot blurring to me. Not sure what monitor you''re using and you may not be seeing it so obviously, but it might pay to look at your image on other screens just to be sure, before uploading :)', '2008-10-27 16:50:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(5027724, 731868, 62318, '<td valign="top">Very nice stag.Looks like he might still be a fairly young guy. Where did you capture this at.</td>', 'Very nice stag.Looks like he might still be a fairly young guy. Where did you capture this at.', '2008-10-27 17:06:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(5027726, 732163, 67145, '<td valign="top">hey steve .. a huge CONGRATULATONS on a brilliant shot and an excellent addition to your profile page .. STUNNING .. !! ..:)</td>', 'hey steve .. a huge CONGRATULATONS on a brilliant shot and an excellent addition to your profile page .. STUNNING .. !! ..:)', '2008-10-27 17:06:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(5027730, 731987, 97270, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by rinac:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Prash:</b></div><hr/><i> Also, just to clarify, if a wildlife challenge happens again in future, with the same description, I will run to the zoo again.. unless the description clearly states ''no zoo pictures allowed''. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Good on ya, me too! Not that mine was at a zoo, just that I have absolutely no problem with it and would do it myself next time.<br/> <br/>As for the photo, I think <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=91527" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Jessi</a> pretty much sums up all the technical/editing issues I had with it also. Those "smudgy" bits she refers to look like spot blurring to me. Not sure what monitor you''re using and you may not be seeing it so obviously, but it might pay to look at your image on other screens just to be sure, before uploading :) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks!<br/> <br/>The spot blurring sources itself to the tiger''s huge tongue on the glass that separated it from us camera junkies. For some reason, he got annoyed with me setting the shot up and taking too long.. so as I was about to click, he smeared the glass with his saliva;-)<br/> <br/>About the crop and over sharpening, I agree.. I should have done better with those.</td>', 'Originally posted by rinac: Originally posted by Prash: Also, just to clarify, if a wildlife challenge happens again in future, with the same description, I will run to the zoo again.. unless the description clearly states ''no zoo pictures allowed''.   Good on ya, me too! Not that mine was at a zoo, just that I have absolutely no problem with it and would do it myself next time. As for the photo, I think  Jessi pretty much sums up all the technical/editing issues I had with it also. Those "smudgy" bits she refers to look like spot blurring to me. Not sure what monitor you''re using and you may not be seeing it so obviously, but it might pay to look at your image on other screens just to be sure, before uploading :)   Thanks! The spot blurring sources itself to the tiger''s huge tongue on the glass that separated it from us camera junkies. For some reason, he got annoyed with me setting the shot up and taking too long.. so as I was about to click, he smeared the glass with his saliva;-) About the crop and over sharpening, I agree.. I should have done better with those.', '2008-10-27 17:09:43.000000', NULL, 0),
