(5028890, 732247, 3936, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on a well deserved blue ribbon.<br/> <br/>I really like the way you used a shallow depth of field to single out the one bird.  Make him/her look like the spokes person for the group.  And although I guess birds don''t really get expressions, the coloring and camera angle are perfect for a ver humerous "expression".</td>', 'Congratulations on a well deserved blue ribbon. I really like the way you used a shallow depth of field to single out the one bird.  Make him/her look like the spokes person for the group.  And although I guess birds don''t really get expressions, the coloring and camera angle are perfect for a ver humerous "expression".', '2008-10-28 10:58:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(5028950, 731868, 59029, '<td valign="top">Very good framing, the light is nice and diffused, and the stag is cooperating with his regal pose and direct stare.  Lucky you to get such a pleasing shot.  I originally remarked on the colour looking a little odd, but I was on another computer.  Looks way better now! :-)</td>', 'Very good framing, the light is nice and diffused, and the stag is cooperating with his regal pose and direct stare.  Lucky you to get such a pleasing shot.  I originally remarked on the colour looking a little odd, but I was on another computer.  Looks way better now! :-)', '2008-10-28 11:56:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(5028951, 732232, 59029, '<td valign="top">Hi Bear!  I am so glad I gave this shot a 9, despite/because of the noise. It''s a lovely shot, great motion, and the textures add an almost otherworldly quality.  Well done, wish it had scored higher!</td>', 'Hi Bear!  I am so glad I gave this shot a 9, despite/because of the noise. It''s a lovely shot, great motion, and the textures add an almost otherworldly quality.  Well done, wish it had scored higher!', '2008-10-28 11:59:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(5028954, 732075, 59029, '<td valign="top">Too frickin funny that this DID turn out to be your shot!  Great focus on the bird and love the use of negative space,and the dof with the distant church spire really adds to the shot.  Great capture Deb!</td>', 'Too frickin funny that this DID turn out to be your shot!  Great focus on the bird and love the use of negative space,and the dof with the distant church spire really adds to the shot.  Great capture Deb!', '2008-10-28 12:01:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(5028966, 731783, 59029, '<td valign="top">I do like this shot, it has a lot of potential. I''m going to download a copy and show you how I''d have cropped it, easier than trying to explain it!<br/> <br/>OK here it is...<a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=734441" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/55000-59999/59029/120/734441.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/55000-59999/59029/120/734441.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/55000-59999/59029/120/734441.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>I cropped it, cloned out the leaf and other misc bits of debris in the water and the very tip of the other cygnet''s beak, and what was visible of a swan in the very top left.  Remember in advanced editing that cloning is allowed!<br/> <br/>Then I did a +10 brightness and +16 contrast over whole pic to make the white swans pop a litle more.<br/> <br/>Then I magic lasso''d the cygnet, +10 contrast on him, then with the lasso still on him, did 1 pass with usm to try and make him pop a little more.<br/> <br/>Hope this helps! :-)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-10-28 12:57:59.</i></td>', 'I do like this shot, it has a lot of potential. I''m going to download a copy and show you how I''d have cropped it, easier than trying to explain it! OK here it is...  I cropped it, cloned out the leaf and other misc bits of debris in the water and the very tip of the other cygnet''s beak, and what was visible of a swan in the very top left.  Remember in advanced editing that cloning is allowed! Then I did a +10 brightness and +16 contrast over whole pic to make the white swans pop a litle more. Then I magic lasso''d the cygnet, +10 contrast on him, then with the lasso still on him, did 1 pass with usm to try and make him pop a little more. Hope this helps! :-)', '2008-10-28 12:10:05.000000', '2008-10-28 12:57:59.000000', 0),
(5028979, 731789, 59029, '<td valign="top">I love the lighting here, great pose, cool subject, and the branch lends interest to the composition. The darkness of the bg still detracts, would be nice to see it lightened.  I gave this one a 7. I don''t know what the Orton effect is, but guess I''d better learn!</td>', 'I love the lighting here, great pose, cool subject, and the branch lends interest to the composition. The darkness of the bg still detracts, would be nice to see it lightened.  I gave this one a 7. I don''t know what the Orton effect is, but guess I''d better learn!', '2008-10-28 12:15:44.000000', NULL, 0),
