(5112480, 731169, 66635, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by jtf6agent:</b></div><hr/><i> I knew most of the up tight A-Holes would butcher the photo because their pea brains refuse to let them think any harder than pressing the 2 key to save their own crap photos. This is pretty easy to figure out. Firefighters live a "Wildlife" This shot was taken on the fly and no processing. I''d like to see half the "photographers" (more like GWC''s) that placed before me try something like this. I''m not sure why I continue to punish myself by entering knowing full well the BS that goes on with DPC voting.  My respect goes out to a few that placed in this challenge and the rest of you box shooters... well I think you know where I stand on that matter. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Wow!  Having read what the challenge required, you''re the only one acting like an A-hole.  The challenge requirements were quite clear and you failed to meet them or even come close.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-12-06 17:57:16.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by jtf6agent: I knew most of the up tight A-Holes would butcher the photo because their pea brains refuse to let them think any harder than pressing the 2 key to save their own crap photos. This is pretty easy to figure out. Firefighters live a "Wildlife" This shot was taken on the fly and no processing. I''d like to see half the "photographers" (more like GWC''s) that placed before me try something like this. I''m not sure why I continue to punish myself by entering knowing full well the BS that goes on with DPC voting.  My respect goes out to a few that placed in this challenge and the rest of you box shooters... well I think you know where I stand on that matter.   Wow!  Having read what the challenge required, you''re the only one acting like an A-hole.  The challenge requirements were quite clear and you failed to meet them or even come close.', '2008-12-06 17:45:27.000000', '2008-12-06 17:57:16.000000', 0),
(5112766, 731169, 59029, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by OmanOtter:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by jtf6agent:</b></div><hr/><i> I knew most of the up tight A-Holes would butcher the photo because their pea brains refuse to let them think any harder than pressing the 2 key to save their own crap photos. This is pretty easy to figure out. Firefighters live a "Wildlife" This shot was taken on the fly and no processing. I''d like to see half the "photographers" (more like GWC''s) that placed before me try something like this. I''m not sure why I continue to punish myself by entering knowing full well the BS that goes on with DPC voting.  My respect goes out to a few that placed in this challenge and the rest of you box shooters... well I think you know where I stand on that matter. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Wow!  Having read what the challenge required, you''re the only one acting like an A-hole.  The challenge requirements were quite clear and you failed to meet them or even come close. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>What he said, Nick.  I for one never ever deliberately vote down others shots in the stupid and vain hope that it will make my score rise - cause it doesn''t work! They get scrubbed! Give out worthwhile scores/comments, get the same back.<br/> <br/>Or are you just p.o.''d that you and your experience and big-ass lens and camera combined can''t beat people with beginner-level DSLRs?  Am I one of the recipients of your spiteful little 2s?  I am very, very hard-pressed to ever give out anything less than a 4.<br/> <br/>And the whole thing with <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=88136" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Jdubsgirl</a>...pitiful.  Truly.<br/> <br/>If you don''t enjoy photography, and are still sooo delicate and precious that you can''t accept criticism, then dpc will be all the richer for your departure.</td>', 'Originally posted by OmanOtter: Originally posted by jtf6agent: I knew most of the up tight A-Holes would butcher the photo because their pea brains refuse to let them think any harder than pressing the 2 key to save their own crap photos. This is pretty easy to figure out. Firefighters live a "Wildlife" This shot was taken on the fly and no processing. I''d like to see half the "photographers" (more like GWC''s) that placed before me try something like this. I''m not sure why I continue to punish myself by entering knowing full well the BS that goes on with DPC voting.  My respect goes out to a few that placed in this challenge and the rest of you box shooters... well I think you know where I stand on that matter.   Wow!  Having read what the challenge required, you''re the only one acting like an A-hole.  The challenge requirements were quite clear and you failed to meet them or even come close.   What he said, Nick.  I for one never ever deliberately vote down others shots in the stupid and vain hope that it will make my score rise - cause it doesn''t work! They get scrubbed! Give out worthwhile scores/comments, get the same back. Or are you just p.o.''d that you and your experience and big-ass lens and camera combined can''t beat people with beginner-level DSLRs?  Am I one of the recipients of your spiteful little 2s?  I am very, very hard-pressed to ever give out anything less than a 4. And the whole thing with  Jdubsgirl...pitiful.  Truly. If you don''t enjoy photography, and are still sooo delicate and precious that you can''t accept criticism, then dpc will be all the richer for your departure.', '2008-12-06 20:01:12.000000', NULL, 0),
